What is actually linked
-----------------------

This list is not guessed: it comes from the linker map of the release build
(-Wl,-Map). Besides askmdb's own code, the binary is built from:

  - llama.cpp: libllama.a, libggml.a, libggml-base.a, libggml-cpu.a and
    libggml-vulkan.a (CPU and Vulkan backends; no other GPU backends, no
    network code, no OpenMP). Inside libggml-cpu.a, sgemm.cpp (tinyBLAS)
    and ops.cpp (YaRN) carry their own notices, reproduced below.
    libggml-vulkan.a also holds ggml's Vulkan compute shaders, compiled to
    SPIR-V at build time and embedded as byte arrays; they are generated
    from ggml's own shader sources and are covered by the llama.cpp / ggml
    license.
  - MongoDB C Driver: libmongoc2.a and libbson2.a, configured with only what
    askmdb needs: TLS through OpenSSL, SCRAM authentication and DNS SRV
    lookups for mongodb+srv:// URIs. It is built without compression
    (snappy, zlib, zstd), without Cyrus SASL / Kerberos and without
    client-side encryption (no libmongocrypt, no kms-message). The pieces of
    bundled third-party code that end up in the binary are jsonsl (in
    libbson), common-b64.c, common-md5.c, mongoc-memcmp.c and utf8proc
    (used to prepare SCRAM-SHA-256 passwords). Their notices are reproduced
    below. The driver's other bundled code (zlib, uthash, kms-message, the
    Windows Secure Channel TLS code) is not linked.
  - OpenSSL 3.5.9: libssl.a and libcrypto.a, built from the official source
    release as static libraries only (no-shared, no-module: the default
    providers are inside libcrypto.a). It is used for TLS connections to
    MongoDB and for SCRAM. askmdb does not read the system openssl.cnf.
  - nlohmann/json, from llama.cpp's vendor/ directory. It is header-only,
    so its code is compiled into askmdb's own object files.
  - Vulkan-Headers (tag vulkan-sdk-1.4.357.0, which includes vulkan.hpp)
    and SPIRV-Headers (commit 04fd3caa). They are header-only: their inline
    code, types and constants are compiled into the object files of
    ggml-vulkan and of askmdb's own Vulkan shim.
  - GCC 13 runtime, linked statically (-static-libstdc++ -static-libgcc):
    libstdc++.a, libgcc.a, libgcc_eh.a and the crtbeginS.o / crtendS.o
    startup files.
  - glibc, linked dynamically (libc.so.6, libm.so.6, libpthread.so.0,
    libdl.so.2, librt.so.1, libresolv.so.2, ld-linux-x86-64.so.2), plus its
    small startup objects (Scrt1.o, crti.o, crtn.o, libc_nonshared.a).
    glibc itself is provided by the user's system.

The Vulkan loader (libvulkan) is not linked: the binary has no dependency
on it. When askmdb uses the GPU, its own shim (part of askmdb, MIT) opens
libvulkan.so.1 with dlopen at run time. The loader is provided by the
user's system and is not distributed with askmdb.

Nothing else from llama.cpp's vendor/ directory is linked (no cpp-httplib,
miniaudio, stb, sheredom or the hash libraries).

Build tools such as glslc (from shaderc, with glslang and SPIRV-Tools) and
ggml's vulkan-shaders-gen run only while building. They are not part of the
binary and are not distributed.


